          "explanation": {
            "content": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "There are three ethylenediamine (en) ligands present. This ligand contains "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "di"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in its name, so the prefix "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "tris"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "- is used to indicate three en molecules. "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2827230248",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "En is neutral, and the complex has a charge of +2, so the charge on Ni is also +2. Since the complex ion is a cation, this is named nickel(II)."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1163296450",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "This name of the complex is therefore tris(ethylenediamine)nickel(II) ion."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "978289947",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
